\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces Cross-tier synthesis of the three validation tiers. The shared inverse-MC scoring core of \cref  {sec:disc-cross-tier} produces every row; the loader, regime definition, and OD-control logic differ by tier. Tier~2 is the representative seed~$42$ at $T=20$ (\cref  {tab:phase4-features}); Tier~3 is the pooled Apr~17--21 pool at $T=10$ (\cref  {tab:phase5-headline}), plus the Labour-Day stress test at $K=64$ where shown. Fitted and Pearson cells are \texttt  {none}/\texttt  {real}. $^{\dagger }$Tier~1 is a $\pi $-recovery reproduction scored by RMAE, not a detection AUC: best RMAE $0.19$ at $|X_o|=70$, within $\sim 0.05$ of the paper's Fig.~2A (\cref  {tab:phase1-rmae}). $^{\ddagger }$The Tier-3 ceiling shown is the un-matched $5$-day pool. OD-matching at $K=8$ lowers it to $0.518$, but a granularity sweep $K \in \{8, 16, 32, 64\}$ returns the matched reference to $\sim \!0.55$--$0.58$ for $K \ge 16$, so no fixed OD-mix fraction is claimed; the fitted detector stays at chance across all $K$ (\cref  {tab:phase5-ksweep}). $^{\S  }$Labour Day vs.\ normal days, OD-matched at $K=64$: $\mathrm  {AUC}_{\mathrm  {emp}}=0.567$, zero-init $\mathrm  {AUC}_{\mathrm  {fit}}=0.521$, multistart validation-selected $\mathrm  {AUC}_{\mathrm  {fit}}=0.502$, Pearson $+0.066$; a fitting-free $2$-step empirical backoff diagnostic does not improve the reference (best non-degenerate setting below $0.567$; \cref  {tab:phase5-labour}). The Tier-2 Pearson lift is robust across five seeds ($\Delta = +0.050 \pm 0.023$, $p \approx 0.008$, \cref  {sec:phase4-multiseed}).}}{34}{table.caption.41}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:cross-tier}{{13}{34}{Cross-tier synthesis of the three validation tiers. The shared inverse-MC scoring core of \cref {sec:disc-cross-tier} produces every row; the loader, regime definition, and OD-control logic differ by tier. Tier~2 is the representative seed~$42$ at $T=20$ (\cref {tab:phase4-features}); Tier~3 is the pooled Apr~17--21 pool at $T=10$ (\cref {tab:phase5-headline}), plus the Labour-Day stress test at $K=64$ where shown. Fitted and Pearson cells are \code {none}/\code {real}. $^{\dagger }$Tier~1 is a $\pi $-recovery reproduction scored by RMAE, not a detection AUC: best RMAE $0.19$ at $|X_o|=70$, within $\sim 0.05$ of the paper's Fig.~2A (\cref {tab:phase1-rmae}). $^{\ddagger }$The Tier-3 ceiling shown is the un-matched $5$-day pool. OD-matching at $K=8$ lowers it to $0.518$, but a granularity sweep $K \in \{8, 16, 32, 64\}$ returns the matched reference to $\sim \!0.55$--$0.58$ for $K \ge 16$, so no fixed OD-mix fraction is claimed; the fitted detector stays at chance across all $K$ (\cref {tab:phase5-ksweep}). $^{\S }$Labour Day vs.\ normal days, OD-matched at $K=64$: $\AUC _{\mathrm {emp}}=0.567$, zero-init $\AUC _{\mathrm {fit}}=0.521$, multistart validation-selected $\AUC _{\mathrm {fit}}=0.502$, Pearson $+0.066$; a fitting-free $2$-step empirical backoff diagnostic does not improve the reference (best non-degenerate setting below $0.567$; \cref {tab:phase5-labour}). The Tier-2 Pearson lift is robust across five seeds ($\Delta = +0.050 \pm 0.023$, $p \approx 0.008$, \cref {sec:phase4-multiseed})}{table.caption.41}{}}
\newlabel{tab:cross-tier@cref}{{[table][13][]13}{[1][33][]34}{}{}{}}
